{"ts": "2026-11-21T08:10:59.566292Z", "run_id": "r-20261121T0805Z-2be7", "unit": "openspec:add-run-view", "seq": 10, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-007", "id": "Q-007", "status": "answered", "reason": "The unit's e2e test traces the criterion and asserts each THEN clause line by line; RunPage.tsx, run-view.ts and runs.css implement each. The missing red record is procedural (AGENTS.md: a red step runs only the Node gate). The generated test's mocks do not match the API paths and shapes the web client uses (runs-source.ts, types.ts, people.ts), which explains its failure at head independently of the code. I could not run the e2e gate myself.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "H-e730fe4b", "kind": "verdict", "batch": "Q-007+3", "batch_size": 3, "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.083738, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "c45a31b08ed87b6fe723c51f33a74f2caa37b75944e27c3bf0a023bcf8825e74", "checked": [{"ref": "e2e/test_m6b_run_view.py:160", "quote": "@pytest.mark.l4(\"C-b43a5bfb\")", "claim": "The unit's browser test is tagged with the criterion id."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m6b_run_view.py:174", "quote": "expect(status).to_have_text(\"State: completed\")", "claim": "The test asserts the status text of the scenario."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m6b_run_view.py:190", "quote": "assert sorted(first) == [f\"{n:064x}\" for n in (1, 2, 3)]", "claim": "The test asserts exactly the three output digests were read."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m6b_run_view.py:208", "quote": "assert abs(details_box[\"y\"] - timeline_box[\"y\"]) <= 8", "claim": "The test asserts Step details and Timeline sit side by side within 8 px."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m6b_run_view.py:213", "quote": "expect(page.get_by_role(\"tooltip\")).to_have_text(\"2026-11-17 10:00 UTC\")", "claim": "The test asserts the exact start time as the tooltip on focus."}, {"ref": "web/src/runs/RunPage.tsx:228", "quote": "<p role=\"status\" aria-label=\"Run state\" data-tone={header.tone} className=\"runs-state\">", "claim": "The page renders the Run state status with data-tone from the header view."}, {"ref": "web/src/runs/RunPage.tsx:130", "quote": "if (requested.has(ref)) return Promise.resolve();", "claim": "A ref already requested is never fetched twice, so each digest is read once."}, {"ref": "web/src/runs/RunPage.tsx:270", "quote": "{row.preview === null ? null : <p className=\"runs-preview\">{row.preview}</p>}", "claim": "Each step with a preview renders it in p.runs-preview."}, {"ref": "web/src/runs/RunPage.tsx:292", "quote": "<time dateTime={cell.iso} title={cell.iso}>", "claim": "Started and Ended detail cells render as a time element with dateTime and title."}, {"ref": "web/src/runs/runs.css:64", "quote": "grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);", "claim": "From 80rem the layout has two equal columns."}, {"ref": "web/src/runs/runs-source.ts:78", "quote": "/runs/${runId}/payloads/${sha256}", "claim": "The payload route the client calls is the one the unit's test mocks, not the one the generated test mocked."}, {"ref": "web/src/runs/types.ts:8", "quote": "const DIGEST_PATTERN = /^[0-9a-f]{64}$/;", "claim": "Step refs must be 64-hex digests, so the generated test's refs could not parse."}, {"ref": "AGENTS.md:93", "quote": "A red step runs only the Node gate", "claim": "The project's rules make a red record for a browser test impossible, so the gap is procedural."}]}
